<h1>Find a state-accredited lab to test your well water</h1>
<p class="lead">If you have a private well, nobody tests your water for you. States publish lists of accredited labs, but they are scattered across PDFs and search forms with different layouts. We collect them into one place, link every listing to the state source, and show the date we last checked it.</p>
<h2>Start with your state</h2>
<ul class="cards">
{% for key, d in labs %}
  <li><h3><a href="/labs/{{ key }}/">{{ states[key].name }}</a></h3>
  <p class="small">{{ d.labs.length }} labs listed · source list: {{ d.list_source.report_date }}</p></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>More states are on the way. If yours is not here, EPA keeps a <a href="https://www.epa.gov/dwlabcert/contact-information-certification-programs-and-certified-laboratories-drinking-water" rel="noopener">directory of each state's lab certification program</a>.</p>
<h2>Guides</h2>
